# Codex and Claude run on the user's machines

`codex_*` and `claude_send` talk only to a **local** Unix socket on the machine
where the process runs. gbot has **no remote transport**.

- Codex/Claude sessions live on the user's registered computers (Linux desktop,
  Mac, …), not on the Grok Bot agent box (`HOME=/home/box`, no Codex install).
- When you are on the box, **do not** call those MCP tools. Run the `gbot` CLI on
  the user's machine through **Grok Bot Shell with a machineId** (the host's
  machine-targeted shell).
- On that machine, start the daemon with `codex app-server daemon start` (or
  bootstrap) so `$CODEX_HOME/app-server-control/app-server-control.sock` exists.
- Auth stays with each machine's native Codex or Claude login. Do not invent
  token files or export credentials.
